Just a thought on the impending release:

Will the LaTeX 2e distribution come with a manual?
I hope so!

Frank:  my instinct tells me that because Addison-Wesley
will be publishing your book, they won't let you
distribute the source (so that we can all print our
own copy).  Am I right?

If so, what sort of documentation can we expect?

In the meantime, would someone please provide a list
of all the new features (commands & what they do)?
I would like to link the installation of the software
with a seminar to let my users know what they're letting
themselves in for.  If I have this information *before*
the release I will be able to prepare a talk beforehand,
so that the users can get started right away.

Richard.

